sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User (Browser)
    participant Client as Next.js React UI
    participant BFF as Next.js BFF Server
    participant API as Go Chi Monolith
    participant DB as PostgreSQL 17

    User->>Client: Types "aanya" in workspace search
    Client->>Client: Debounce timer waits 250ms

    Client->>BFF: GET /api/users/search?q=aanya
    BFF->>API: GET /v1/users?q=aanya (Forwarding Cookie)

    API->>API: Verify session cookie & check search rate limit
    alt Rate limit exceeded (>60/min)
        API-->>BFF: 429 Too Many Requests (Retry-After)
        BFF-->>Client: 429 Problem Details
        Client-->>User: Display calm rate-limit message
    else Allowed
        API->>DB: SearchUsers(caller_id, query="aanya", limit=10)
        Note over DB: Evaluates GIN Trigram Index & joins follows table
        DB-->>API: Return candidate rows [Aanya Sharma (@aanya)]
        API-->>BFF: 200 OK { users: [...] }
        BFF-->>Client: 200 OK JSON
        Client-->>User: Render search candidate card
    end

    User->>Client: Clicks on @aanya candidate
    Client->>BFF: Fetch public profile /v1/users/aanya
    BFF->>API: GET /v1/users/aanya (Cookie)
    API->>DB: GetPublicProfileWithRelationship(caller_id, "aanya")
    DB-->>API: Return profile + is_following + counts
    API-->>BFF: 200 OK { publicProfile }
    BFF-->>Client: 200 OK
    Client-->>User: Open UserProfileModal (Avatar, Bio, Follow button)

    User->>Client: Clicks "Follow" button
    Client->>BFF: Server Action: followUserAction("aanya")
    BFF->>API: POST /v1/users/aanya/follow (Cookie, CSRF, Origin)
    API->>DB: INSERT INTO follows (follower, following) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    DB-->>API: 204 No Content
    API-->>BFF: 204 No Content
    BFF-->>Client: State updated: isFollowing = true
    Client-->>User: Button transforms to "Following" (accent styling)
    Note over User,DB: Milestone 4 Boundary: Following creates a directional relationship edge only; it does NOT initiate a conversation or grant direct messaging permissions.
